mode script

// Regression: an owned Dynamic declared from an erased-dynamic source (a
// deref() result bound by ref) must copy the POINTER WORD. The
// interpreter's clone path assumed every Dynamic binding is a boxed slot
// and deref'd the raw allocation itself, boxing a garbage word that the
// later free(own ...) then freed -- interpreter-only segfault; compiled
// mode copies the word and frees the real block.

// The block is allocated in argument position on purpose: naming it in a
// binding would leave that binding owning it after the free-through-alias
// below, and session teardown would free it a second time (#275's
// double-ownership, a separate limitation).
slot : U8 = malloc(UPtr.size())
write_ptr(slot, malloc(4))
ref back : Dynamic = deref(slot)
recovered : Dynamic = back
free(own recovered)
free(own slot)
println("ok")
